  "legacyId": "9622e42d-866b-4524-a9dd-f57017f71a1b",
  "type": "problem",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "description": "<div>\n  <p>In a map of zeros (water) and ones (land), the area of an island is its number of connected land cells. Return the greatest area, or zero when there is no land.</p>\n  <p>Unlike counting islands, the size of each component matters.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[1,1,0],[0,1,0],[1,0,1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3</pre>\n  <p>The three connected cells at the top form the largest island.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[0,0],[0,0]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 0</pre>\n  <p>Every cell is water.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> grid = [[1]]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1</pre>\n  <p>A single land cell has area one.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>0 &lt;= rows, columns &lt;= 100</code>; an empty grid has no islands.</li>\n    <li>All rows have equal length; cells have the values stated above.</li>\n    <li>Only side-sharing cells are adjacent; diagonal contact does not connect them.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
  "templates": {
    "python": "class Solution:\n    def maxAreaOfIsland(self, grid: List[List[int]]):\n        \"\"\"NUMBER\"\"\"\n        pass\n",
    "javascript": "class Solution {\n  /** Return the required number result. */\n  maxAreaOfIsland(grid) {\n    // your code here\n  }\n}\n"
  },
